  "portal_description": "Red Hat Satellite is a system management solution that allows organizations to configure and maintain their systems without necessity to provide public Internet access to their servers or other client systems. It also performs provisioning and configuration management of predefined standard operating environments.\n\nRed Hat Satellite 6 integrates several other projects that provide particular functionalities in Provisioning and Configuration Management, and Content and Subscription Management. The following projects are the most fundamental: Katello, Foreman, Candlepin, Pulp, and Puppet. \n\nKatello is a subscription and repository management application that enables users to subscribe to Red Hat repositories and download the content. Foreman is an open source application responsible for provisioning, configuration and life cycle management of the systems. Candlepin is a software collection used by Katello to handle subscription management. Pulp is a service used by Katello to handle repository and content management. And Puppet is an automation software used to handle provisioning and configuration tasks.\n\nThis update delivers client agents for newly-released Red Hat Satellite 6.0 on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 5, 6, and 7 systems.\n  \nAll users of Red Hat Satellite are advised to install this newly released version of client agents.",
